Here's what I mean when I say it is not possible.  Consider the
classic case of putting a WoCancel in a BoH.  It is possible to do
this by typing the wrong letter when attempting to put something else
in - a typo.  It is possible to do this because you don't yet know
that this is a bad idea - a lack of knowlege.  Or, it is possible to
do this even knowing what usually happens, because you are hastilly
trying to get unburdened or make room, and don't care what you stick
in the bag - a lapse of judgement.  But these all require the exact
same keystrokes.  If you give a confirmation to prevent the typo,
you'll also usually prevent the others.

I suppose you could allow the user to completely define their own set
of confirmations.  That way you wouldn't be spoiling them at all. 
That would get around the problem.  It would actually be a pretty cool
feature.  But I fear that it would still be too cumbersome for most
people to use much, and a pain to code besides.

